// What ACTUALLY runs locally — docker-compose, 11 containers.
//
// Paste into https://app.eraser.io as a Cloud Architecture diagram.
//
// This is deliberately a SEPARATE diagram from 01-system-architecture. That one
// is the target; this one is the artefact. Drawing both as one picture is how an
// architecture diagram starts lying: the differences below are real and every
// one of them is a known alpha gap, not a simplification worth hiding.
//
//   RF=1 on Kafka             — a single broker cannot survive losing it
//   no TLS anywhere           — plaintext between every hop
//   one ClickHouse, no replicas
//   MinIO stands in for S3
//   one Postgres serves BOTH the control plane and the demo app's own schema
//
// Ports are host-side, as published in docker-compose.yml.

title Local Topology — docker-compose (the artefact, not the target)

Demo [icon: terminal, color: green] {
  Demo Server [label: "demo_server\nMCP server on stdio or HTTP", icon: python]
  Partner APIs [label: "mock partner APIs\npayments :8801 · inventory :8802 · shipping :8803\nfast / slow / flaky — nothing calls the internet", icon: cloud]
}

Ingest Path [icon: log-in, color: red] {
  Ingest [label: "ingest :4319\nFastAPI · auth · quota · tenant stamping", icon: lock]
  Collector [label: "otel-collector\nOTLP :4318/:4317 · health :13133 · metrics :8889", icon: layers]
  Kafka [label: "kafka :9092\nKRaft · RF=1 ⚠ · otlp.spans.raw", icon: kafka, color: purple]
  Kafka Init [label: "kafka-init\none-shot topic creation", icon: play, color: gray]
}

Processing [icon: cpu, color: blue] {
  Normalizer [label: "normalizer\nOTLP decode → MCP fields → failure taxonomy", icon: filter]
  Archiver [label: "archiver\nparquet → object store", icon: archive]
}

Storage [icon: database, color: yellow] {
  ClickHouse [label: "clickhouse :8123 / :9000\nspans_raw + rollups · single node", icon: database]
  Postgres [label: "postgres :5433\ncontrol plane AND demo_app schema", icon: postgresql]
  Redis [label: "redis :6379\nquotas · principal cache", icon: redis]
  MinIO [label: "minio :9002 (console :9001)\nstands in for S3", icon: hard-drive]
  MySQL [label: "mysql :3307\nsecond engine, so db.system is visibly not one value", icon: mysql]
}

Serving [icon: monitor, color: green] {
  Query [label: "query :8080\nQuery API + console", icon: search]
  Docs [label: "mkdocs :8009\ncustomer-facing docs", icon: book]
}

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── flows
Demo Server > Partner APIs: HTTP child spans
Demo Server > Postgres: psycopg — demo_app schema
Demo Server > MySQL: pymysql
Demo Server > Redis: cache read/write
Demo Server > Ingest: "OTLP/HTTP :4319"

Ingest > Collector: forward, tenant stamped
Ingest > Postgres: API key → tenant
Ingest > Redis: quota counters
Kafka Init > Kafka: create topics
Collector > Kafka: acks=all

Kafka > Normalizer
Kafka > Archiver
Normalizer > ClickHouse: batched insert, dedup token
Archiver > MinIO: parquet

Query > ClickHouse
Query > Postgres
